  "title": "Motor imagination and execution with a chronic wireless epidural ECoG BCI (WIMAGINE), one participant with tetraplegia (Pollina et al. 2026)",
  "description": "Chronic wireless epidural electrocorticography (ECoG) recordings from one participant with incomplete C6 tetraplegia implanted with the WIMAGINE device. The participant executed or imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, singly or simultaneously (one executed and one imagined), across eight sessions. The derivative release provides 32 left-hemisphere channels over primary motor and sensory cortex, band-pass filtered at 1-250 Hz, with trial events and electrode anatomical labels, repackaged in iEEG-BIDS.",
  "methods_description": "WIMAGINE wireless epidural ECoG implant (64 planar electrodes, 32 recorded from the left implant over M1/S1) with a 0.5-300 Hz analog band-pass and a 292.8 Hz FIR low-pass, sampled at about 585 Hz. The seated participant followed on-screen instructions to execute or imagine reaching and wrist-extension movements, with EMG monitoring of execution. The authors applied a zero-phase 5th-order Butterworth band-pass of 1-250 Hz.",
